   <text>
      <body>
         <head n="5736b" xml:lang="en">
            <date>99 BC</date>
            <placeName>Oxyrhynchus</placeName>
            <ref n="p.oxy;4;802" type="reprint-from">P.Oxy. 4 802</ref>
            <ref n="sb;6;9255" type="reprint-from">SB 6 9255</ref>
            <ref n="p.ryl;4;586" type="reprint-from">P.Ryl. 4 586</ref>
         </head>
         <div type="commentary" subtype="frontmatter" xml:space="preserve"><p>This is a reconstruction of SB VI 9255 and P.Ryl. IV 586. At line 9 of the text presented here line 9 of SB VI 9255 joins neatly with line 1 of P.Ryl. IV 586 to produce an almost complete text.</p></div>
         <div xml:lang="grc" type="edition" xml:space="preserve">
           <note xml:lang="en">This text has not been added to papyri.info yet.</note>
           <ab/>
         </div>
         <div type="commentary" subtype="linebyline">
            <list>
               <item corresp="#lb7" xml:space="preserve"><ref>7</ref> <p>Λάκων is not a personal name, but rather an ethnic (BL 7.205).</p></item>
               <item corresp="#lb8" xml:space="preserve"><ref>8</ref> <p>There is writing on a small strip of papyrus that hangs from the bottom of the fragment kept in Graz (SB 6.9255) and spans lines 8-12.  It is difficult to reconcile the traces with the supplements given in P.Ryl. 4.586, especially ll. 10 and 12.  Thus, either the supplements are wrong or the placing of the fragment is incorrect.</p></item>
               <item corresp="#lb10" xml:space="preserve"><ref>10-11</ref> <p>For the proposed supplement [ἐπακολουθούντων τῶν] ἀπὸ τοῦ συστή[ματος ἐκ τῶν ἐπὶ], see BL 5.88 (cf. also BL 4.74).</p></item>
            </list>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
